<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine cash grains down in thin trade.</title>
<headline>Argentine cash grains down in thin trade.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine maize and soybeans slipped in thin cash market trade at Buenos Aires Cereals Exchange Tuesday, traders said.</p>
<p>FAS elevator soybeans lost $5 in Rosario to $284, with the market reacting to Monday's fall in Chicago. Monday was a holiday in Argentina. FAS elevator sunflower seed followed soybeans down, slipping to $226 in Rosario. Maize slipped $2 to $106 in Buenos Aires.</p>
<p>(( -- Bueons Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
